`terakan_hw_config_sqk_get_stage_srvs_()` handles every `mesa_shader_stage` it can
be given and signals the rest with an `assert(!"Unsupported shader stage")`.  In
a non-void function that assert is the *only* thing keeping the compiler from
seeing the end of the function, so a build with assertions disabled -- which is
what nixpkgs does, via `-Db_ndebug=true` -- turns the path into undefined
behaviour and trips `-Werror=return-type`:

  ../src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_hw_config_sqk.h:264:1: error:
    control reaches end of non-void function [-Werror=return-type]

`UNREACHABLE()` is Mesa's idiom for exactly this case (util/macros.h documents it
as "useful for suppressing 'control reaches end of non-void function'
warnings"): it still asserts when assertions are enabled, and marks the path
unreachable for the compiler otherwise.

--- 
diff --git a/src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_hw_config_sqk.h b/src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_hw_config_sqk.h
index f5d369c06ad..ada5006f1de 100644
--- a/src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_hw_config_sqk.h
+++ b/src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_hw_config_sqk.h
@@ -259,7 +259,7 @@ terakan_hw_config_sqk_get_stage_srvs_(struct terakan_hw_config_sqk const * const
    case MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE:
       return config->srvs_cs_;
    default:
-      assert(!"Unsupported shader stage");
+      UNREACHABLE("Unsupported shader stage");
    }
 }
 
